## Upstream models

Gatewright's planned agents send prompts to a language model chosen by whoever runs it - a hosted
model under its provider's terms, or a locally run open-weight model (for example through Ollama)
under its own model licence - always through the redactor. The forecast engine runs a tabular model
behind an adapter; its weights are pinned only after licence verification. The lab does not train,
fine-tune or distribute models, and is not a provider of a general-purpose AI model under the EU AI
Act. Obligations for the models themselves sit with their providers.

Output produced with these models is marked per EU AI Act Article 50. See COMPLIANCE.md.

